# The events are written to Es.Api\events.jsonl: open it to see the "database".
# Stop then restart the API: the whole state is rebuilt from this file.
# To start from scratch: delete the file.
@base = http://localhost:5109
@alice = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@bob = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222

### Alice's statement (projection): note the version
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}

### Withdraw 100 €, with a reason
POST {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}/withdrawal
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 100, "reason": "Groceries" }

### Withdraw 300 €
POST {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}/withdrawal
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 300, "reason": "Rent" }

### Transfer from Alice to Bob (two streams, written all or nothing)
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "{{alice}}", "target": "{{bob}}", "amount": 250 }

### Audit: Alice's whole history, immutable
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}/events

### Time travel: Alice as she was at version 2 (after the 1st withdrawal)
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}/state?version=2

### Optimistic concurrency: "I withdraw based on version 1" → 409, because the account changed since
POST {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}/withdrawal
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: 1

{ "amount": 50 }

### Closure refused: the balance is not zero
POST {{base}}/accounts/{{bob}}/closure

### Projection added afterwards: yet it knows all the past withdrawals
GET {{base}}/statistics/largest-withdrawals

### Clear and rebuild all the projections from the first event
POST {{base}}/admin/projections/rebuild

### Content of the store
GET {{base}}/admin/store
